A family meal, a cluttered computer and a phone bill don't sound like big AI projects. That's what makes these Grok Bot stories worth a look: people finding help with things already on their plate.

@0mi202 wanted an easy-to-read guide to In-N-Out's off-menu options for the family. They asked Grok Bot and say it produced a four-page PDF within minutes. It's an unofficial guide, so the choices still need checking, but having something everyone can look through together is a nice little use of it.

@grokademy used a bot to help tidy a 2017 iMac, reporting 967 Downloads files organized and duplicate recovery files moved to Trash. A read-only check came first, and every deletion needed approval. I like that part: getting help with an overdue chore while keeping control of what goes.

@chchdonkey says Grok Bot helped compare flights, electricity suppliers and phone plans, even spotting an email about an upcoming phone-price increase. That's a useful catch. Those notices are easy to miss until the bigger bill arrives.

